## 🛠️ 13. Applying Custom Functions

```python
df["Age_Group"] = df["Age"].apply(lambda x: "Senior" if x > 30 else "Junior")
```
👉 `apply()` runs a function on every value in a column — great for custom transformations.

```python
df.apply(lambda row: row["Age"] * 2, axis=1)  # 🔁 Apply across rows
```

