## ⚡ 15. Quick Tips & Best Practices

- ✅ Always inspect data with `head()`, `info()`, and `describe()` before analysis.
- ✅ Use `copy()` when creating a new DataFrame from a slice → `df2 = df[...].copy()` to avoid warnings.
- ✅ Chain methods for cleaner code:
  ```python
  result = df[df["Age"] > 25].groupby("City")["Salary"].mean().sort_values()
  ```
- ✅ Use `df.reset_index(drop=True)` after filtering/sorting to clean up the index.
- ⚠️ `df["col"] = ...` may trigger a `SettingWithCopyWarning` — use `.loc[]` to be safe:
  ```python
  df.loc[df["Age"] > 25, "Status"] = "Adult"
  ```

